<metadata>

  <!--
    FlushableExecutorService is a Kotlin interface that extends java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService
    and declares one member of its own, drainTo. The generator has to emit an invoker implementing
    every inherited member too, and it gets shutdownNow() wrong: the signature it declares is
    IList<IRunnable>, while the marshalling it emits either side of it uses the non-generic
    JavaList - two errors, CS1503 and CS0266, in code this repository does not write.

    Removing the inherited-interface edge leaves the type itself intact, which matters because it
    is not an isolated helper: it appears as a parameter on the DatadogCore constructor and as the
    return type of FlushableExecutorService.Factory.create, so removing the interface would take
    those members with it.

    The cost is that C# sees FlushableExecutorService without the ExecutorService members, so it
    cannot be implemented from C# to supply a custom executor through the Factory. That is an
    advanced scenario with no MAUI equivalent - the SDK's default back-pressure executor is what
    every app gets - and it is the narrower loss of the two.
  -->
  <remove-node path="/api/package[@name='com.datadog.android.core.thread']/interface[@name='FlushableExecutorService']/implements[@name='java.util.concurrent.ExecutorService']" />

</metadata>
